looks of it this would allow newer shared objects with incompatible ABIs (at least on Linux). Would it be possible to have something more specific?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4065825104/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066173780","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117467#issuecomment-4066173780","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117467","id":4066173780,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yXONU","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T09:12:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T09:12:40Z","body":"> In the current state this PR seems to only include unnecessary style changes (wrappers are generated files, not intended to be readable, and project formatting rules doesn't apply to them, it should be left as it is generated).\r\n\r\nNote that newer releases of dynload-wrapper generate code differently. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98976/changes for example.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066173780/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4072650699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117467#issuecomment-4072650699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117467","id":4072650699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yv7fL","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T06:17:43Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T06:22:14Z","body":"@deralmas @bruvzg Yes I somehow managed to not include the `.c` files. I've added them now but I understand that this may not be the optimal solution. For example, on OpenBSD, what should happen in the wrapper for libX11? The file is libX11.so.19.0, where on Linux it is typically libX11.so.6. Should all platforms fallback to libX11.so.19.0? Should OpenBSD instead only attempt loading libX11.so.19.0 using a `#define`? Can OpenBSD look for the generic libX11.so behind a `#define` (I don't believe these libraries versions are stable on OpenBSD)? Also, do any Linux distros ship libX11 with a version other than libX11.so.6?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4072650699/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4074849586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117467#issuecomment-4074849586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117467","id":4074849586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y4UUy","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T13:11:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T13:11:08Z","body":"@Kaleb-Reid I'm not really sure as I don't know much about BSDs.\r\n\r\nThis article seems to imply that BSDs version their shared libraries: https://begriffs.com/posts/2021-07-04-shared-libraries.html\r\n\r\nAlso this manpage: https://man.openbsd.org/library-specs\r\n\r\nI guess they just have different conventions? Are those consistent between BSDs? If that's the case, I hope that `libX11.so.19` does the job.\r\n\r\n> Also, do any Linux distros ship libX11 with a version other than libX11.so.6?\r\n\r\nNo idea, here I got `libX11.6.4.0`, also symlinked to a generic `libX11.so.6`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4074849586/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078449593","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117467#issuecomment-4078449593","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117467","id":4078449593,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zGDO5","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T22:46:01Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T22:47:01Z","body":"@deralmas OpenBSD definitely has different conventions, as libX11.so.19.0 is libX11-1.8.12, the same version as what I have on Void linux under libX11.so.6.4.0 / libX11.so.6 . I found an SDL commit where they started loading generic versions on OpenBSD: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/11880 .\r\n\r\nX11 components on NetBSD also have different versioning because they bumped them all by one major version 17 years ago: https://github.com/NetBSD/src/commit/6e4e55b07c5115b94d817e62cc9980a8f7176ac8 .\r\n\r\nI've updated the pr to use defines to load a different soname for specific platforms and updated my pr for dynload-wrapper. I also reverted changed I previously made to wrappers which are for libraries not available / I couldn't find on OpenBSD and NetBSD (libdecor and libasound).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078449593/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4079051472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117467#issuecomment-4079051472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117467","id":4079051472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zIWLQ","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T01:34:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T01:34:57Z","body":"I see, thank you for looking into it! Welp, if that's the case, I guess a `#define` is really the best we can do...\r\n\r\nUsing some keywords on your link I found this old patch on the firefox tracker: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/main/src/core/linux/SDL_sandbox.c#L28-L4 . (The issue seems to have been fixed with other patches). So it really looks to be the norm.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I 100% agree with the implementation on the dynload-wrapper side (maybe handling arguments differently or using at least a colon instead of a comma) but that's nitpicking. The general approach looks sound.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4079051472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4079113323","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117467#issuecomment-4079113323","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117467","id":4079113323,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zIlRr","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","fo